  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-AFG133</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workers, in particular the most vulnerable, have been protected from unacceptable forms of work, and child labour has been reduced considerably</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiatives aim to protect Afghanistan&#x2019;s most vulnerable workers from unacceptable forms of work and reduce child labour by strengthening national capacity to uphold fundamental principles and rights at work. Responsive to the changing political and social context, the initiatives focus on improving the understanding and implementation of measures to eliminate the worst forms of child labour, promoting occupational safety and health, and protecting the quality and security of jobs at risk of informality and decent work gaps. The interventions support awareness-raising, rapid assessments, training, and the development of tools and guidelines for preventing child labour and improving working conditions, particularly in micro, small and medium enterprises. They contribute to achieving gender equality and decent work for all by addressing barriers that limit women&#x2019;s and marginalized groups&#x2019; participation in economic activities. Despite challenges such as political instability, restricted women&#x2019;s rights, and limited institutional capacity, the initiatives seek to promote social justice, protect human rights, and create safer, fairer, and more inclusive labour markets in Afghanistan.</narrative>
  </description>
